+**App Store screenshot rule:**
+- Capture App Store screenshots on the Mini.
+- Do not run the capture from a plain SSH shell on the Mini. The app-level screenshot capture scripts auto-reroute through `scripts/mini/mini-gui-run.sh`; keep that behavior intact.
+- Treat Terminal cleanup as part of the capture lane. The shared Mini runner now tags automation windows with `SaneApps Automation:`, reclaims stale windows automatically, and screenshot lanes must request a full reclaim before they capture.
+- If the Mini already looks polluted, run `ssh mini '~/SaneApps/infra/SaneProcess/scripts/mini/mini-reclaim-automation-windows.sh --all --hide-terminal'` before you trust any visual result.
+- Every enabled App Store lane must have both `scripts/capture_appstore_screenshots.sh` and `scripts/validate_appstore_screenshots.sh`.
+- Every enabled App Store lane must have `docs/appstore_screenshot_storyboard.yml`, and that storyboard must still match the screenshot slot order you intend to ship.
+- Use dedicated App Store assets at Apple-accepted sizes. Do not upload undersized website art and rely on App Store Connect scaling.
+- Audit every screenshot against the live app before upload. Each screenshot must make sense on its own, show the intended feature clearly, and represent the current product truthfully.
+- Reject any screenshot that is blurry, off-spec, stale, contaminated by Terminal/browser/dev UI, or cropped so tightly that the feature loses context.
+- If screenshot text includes a price or upgrade CTA, it must come from the app’s current runtime/display price label, not a hardcoded screenshot string.
+- Run the app’s screenshot capture script first, then `./scripts/SaneMaster.rb appstore_preflight`, before any screenshot-only or metadata-only App Store sync.
+- `appstore_submit.rb` must pass the app-level screenshot validator before any screenshot upload, including `--screenshots-only`.
+- After App Store metadata or screenshots change, run the shared live-page audit:
+  - `ruby ~/SaneApps/infra/SaneProcess/scripts/appstore_public_screenshot_audit.rb --project-root /path/to/app`
+  - Do not call the lane healthy until that report shows the public page matching the storyboard/local set.
+  - Open the generated HTML report and compare the actual images side by side. Matching basenames are not enough if the live image still contains old pixels or old pricing.
+- If `appstore_submit.rb --screenshots-only` hits ASC `INVALID_STATE` / `Can't Delete Screenshot After Submit for review`, the lane is locked. Do not keep retrying. A live screenshot replacement now requires a new App Store version.
+- After any pricing, paywall, or App Store copy change, verify parity in this order before shipping:
+  1. `.saneprocess`
+  2. in-app runtime/display price labels
+  3. regenerated screenshots + validator
+  4. App Store Connect IAP price
+  5. live public App Store page
+  6. website/direct pricing copy
+- Do not call the rollout complete until the live public App Store page matches the canonical price/copy and the screenshots are visibly sharp.
+- If a screenshot is accurate but weak, replace it. A screenshot that does not explain the feature or why it matters is not release-ready.
+- Late screenshot QA is too late. If the current public page is wrong and the lane is already `READY_FOR_SALE`, queue the corrected assets into the very next version instead of treating it like a metadata-only fix.
+
